          "filename": "Men To the Left, Women To the Right Please, Towers of Silence, Yazd, Iran (15332440078).jpg",
          "caption": "A \"Tower of Silence\" is a circular, raised structure used by Zoroastrians for exposure of the dead, particularly to scavenging birds for the purposes of excarnation, the practice of removing the flesh and organs of the dead, leaving only the bones. Ancient Zoroastrian beliefs precluded burial or cremation of the dead because they opposed any contamination of earth or air caused by such practices.\n\nen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakhma",
